   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 118 of the laws of 1969, relating to a separate union free school district in the town of Greenburgh, in the county of Westchester, in relation to clarifying the authority of the Greenburgh North Castle Union Free School District to lease certain properties and to expand its boundaries",
    "basePrintNo": "S5829",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5829-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2-a, add §2-c. Chap 118 of 1969",
    "lawSection": "Westchester County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5829\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:    An  act  to amend chapter 118 of the laws of 1969,\nrelating to a separate union free  school  district  in  the  town  of\nGreenburgh,  in  the  county of Westchester, in relation to clarifying\nthe authority  of  the  Greenburgh  North  Castle  Union  Free  School\nDistrict to lease certain properties and to expand its boundaries\n\nPURPOSE  OR  GENERAL  IDEA  OF  BILL:  The  purpose of this bill is to\nauthorize the Greenburgh North Castle union free  school  district  to\nlease  properties  and  expand  its  boundaries  for  the  purpose  of\nproviding instruction to students in the Greenburgh North Castle union\nfree school district,\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: Section 2-a authorizes the  lease  and\nexpansion of boundaries of properties located at 108 Shonnard Place in\nthe  city  of  Yonkers, county of Westchester, and at 1700 Old Orchard\nPlace in the village  of  Valhalla,  county  of  Westchester  for  the\npurpose  of  providing  instruction to students enrolled in the school\ndistrict.\n\nSection 2-b authorizes  the  lease  and  expansion  of  boundaries  of\nproperties  located at 623 Blooming Grove Turnpike, in the town of New\nWindsor, county of Orange, to be known as the  Kaplan  Center  Academy\nfor  the  purpose of providing instruction to students enrolled in the\nschool district.\n\nSection 3 states that Chapter 118 of the laws of 1969  is  amended  by\nadding  a  new  section  2-c.  Section  2-c of the bill authorizes the\nGreenburgh  North  Castle  union  free  school  district,  subject  to\napproval  of  the  New  York  State  education  department,  to  lease\nproperties and expand boundaries of  properties  located  at  45  East\nGainsborg   Avenue   in  the  village  of  West  Harrison,  county  of\nWestchester to be known as the REACH Academy and  to  enter  into  any\nagreements  necessary  for  the  purpose  of  providing instruction to\nstudents enrolled in the Greenburgh North  Castle  union  free  school\ndistrict\n\nSection 4 ratifies, validates and confirms the actions of the board of\neducation  of  the  Greenburgh  North  Castle  union  free district in\nentering into a lease of  properties  located  at  45  East  Gainsborg\nAvenue  notwithstanding  its  location  outside of the school district\nboundaries.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This legislation is necessary to allow the  Greenburgh\nNorth Castle Union Free School District to lease properties and expand\ntheir school boundaries.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  New Bill - 2013\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
